# Visual Mood Lab — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development. None of these are
# required to run locally — with everything unset, the app runs on PGlite
# (an embedded Postgres, no credentials needed) and stores uploads on disk
# under public/uploads/. Set these when you're ready to point at real
# infrastructure, typically when deploying to Vercel.

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Postgres connection string, e.g. from Neon (neon.tech — the free tier
# is enough for this app). Unset: falls back to PGlite at ./.pglite/.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# --- Blob storage ------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Vercel Blob read/write token. Create a Blob store in your Vercel
# project's Storage tab and copy the token it gives you. Unset: uploads
# and generated posters are written to public/uploads/ instead — fine for
# local development, but Vercel's filesystem is read-only in production,
# so this MUST be set before deploying anything that uploads media or
# generates posters.
#
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# --- Seeding -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# The /api/seed route is disabled in production unless this is set. Set it
# temporarily, deploy, visit /api/seed once in a browser to load the
# starter library, then unset it and redeploy (or just leave it disabled —
# there's rarely a reason to reseed a live deployment).
#
# ALLOW_SEED_ROUTE=
